# tests/commit, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating this
# directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A WORKER TEST. The subject is commit-worker.rs — a source-built worker that
# reads a `:commit=` arg, walks its tree and parent by hash, runs one tool call
# through run-then, and mints a child commit. Git was here to MAKE the head
# commit and to READ the child; `caos put-commit` does the first and a
# commit-kind result arrives as raw object bytes, which is the second.
#
# `--rustc:@=DEEP-DEPS/rustc` hands this worker the BUILT builder image: naming
# a dependency evaluates it, so a worker never has to.
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --worker1:@=worker.sh --rustc:@=DEEP-DEPS/rustc --cworker:@=commit-worker.rs --tool:@=tool.sh
